## Execution Patterns (speed + accuracy)

```
✓ parallel grep/glob/Read in DISCOVER
✓ parallel git status + git diff + git log for commits/PRs
✓ Task explore for wide discovery (readonly)
✓ background shell for long build/test
✓ brqosh-agents for large waves — never parallel-mutate same files
✓ re-read after every StrReplace
✓ dotnet test after any behavior change
✓ impact-before-change before Write/StrReplace · MEM + LEARN after verify
✓ grep PROJECT-MEMORY.yaml + skill-lessons.yaml before "we already fixed this"
✓ verify parent directory exists before mkdir/write
✗ drive-by refactor · new dependency without request · suggest instead of execute
✗ git reset --hard · git checkout -- · revert user changes
✗ amend commit unless explicitly requested
```

**Dirty worktree:** never revert changes you did not make. Read and integrate if in files you touch.

